  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Setup**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that `react-syntax-highlighter` compiles and builds without a hitch. Now, I\'m diving into the design and feature requirements. I\'m focusing on the general layout. The goal is an ultra-light gray background, perhaps similar to Notion, with a fixed header, which makes it easier to use.\n\n\n**Defining the UI Elements**\n\nNow, I\'m fleshing out the UI components, starting with a clear structure: a header with a title, subtitle, and search bar. Below this, I\'m designing a filter system with pill-shaped buttons to categorize content. Cards will be arranged responsively in a grid, featuring white backgrounds, rounded corners, and subtle hover shadows. Each card includes a title and a category badge. I\'m leveraging `react-syntax-highlighter` for the code blocks, considering `vscDarkPlus` or `dracula` themes, and adding a copy-to-clipboard button. The dataset will be a separate JSON file.\n\n\n**Enhancing the Feature Set**\n\nI\'m now focusing on high-value enhancements to make this a top-tier product. I\'m prioritizing an interactive search experience with keyboard shortcuts, real-time match counters, clear search buttons, and keyword highlighting. I\'m also planning to implement category badges with distinct color coding for easy visual identification. Finally, I\'ll add a favorites or bookmarking feature.\n\n\n**Adding Advanced Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating crucial advanced features. I\'m focusing on \"Favoris\" functionality, including a star icon on each card for saving to local storage and a \"\342\255\220 Favoris (N)\" filter. I\'m also designing a full-screen/zoom modal for card inspection, and considering \"R\303\251sultat attendu\" accordions for output previews. Moreover, I\'m working on one-click copy actions. I\'m also preparing theme selectors for code blocks and quick print/export capabilities.\n\n\n**Structuring the Data**\n\nI\'m now focusing on organizing the data, ensuring it aligns perfectly with the user\'s prompt. I\'ve designed a structure with categories and items, totaling 16 entries. I will keep the original properties intact and have considered adding metadata. I am also making sure the data will be a JSON array, as requested. I\'ll create a dedicated file with the final `CHEAT_SHEET_DATA`. The next step is to create the header component.\n\n```tsx\n// src/components/Header.tsx\nimport React, { useState } from \'react\';\n\nconst Header: React.FC = () => {\n    // State for the search input\n    const [searchTerm, setSearchTerm] = useState(\'\');\n\n    // Handler for search input changes\n    const handleSearchChange = (e: React.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) => {\n        setSearchTerm(e.target.value);\n        // Implement search logic here\n    };\n\n    // Handler for clearing the search input\n    const handleClearSearch = () => {\n        setSearchTerm(\'\');\n        // Optionally clear the search results\n    };\n\n    return (\n        <header className=\"fixed top-0 left-0 w-full bg-gray-100 p-4 shadow-md z-10\">\n            <div className=\"container mx-auto flex items-center justify-between\">\n                <div className=\"flex items-center\">\n                    {/* Placeholder for Logo */}\n                    <span className=\"text-2xl font-bold mr-4\">Logo</span>\n                    <div>\n                        <h1 className=\"text-xl font-bold\">Cheat Sheet</h1>\n                        <p className=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">Quick Reference Guide</p>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n                <div className=\"flex items-center\">\n                    <input\n                        type=\"text\"\n                        className=\"rounded-md border p-2 mr-2 w-64 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-500\"\n                        placeholder=\"Search...\"\n                        value={searchTerm}\n                        onChange={handleSearchChange}\n                    />\n                    <button\n                        className=\"bg-gray-300 hover:bg-gray-400 text-gray-800 font-bold py-2 px-4 rounded focus:outline-none focus:shadow-outline\"\n                        onClick={handleClearSearch}\n                    >\n                        Clear\n                    </button>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </header>\n    );\n};\n\nexport default Header;\n```\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_138324"
      name: "create_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Content\":\"export interface CategoryInfo {\\n  name: string;\\n  label: string;\\n  color: {\\n    bg: string;\\n    text: string;\\n    border: string;\\n    badgeBg: string;\\n    badgeText: string;\\n    dot: string;\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport const CATEGORY_STYLES: Record<string, CategoryInfo[\'color\']> = {\\n  Bases: {\\n    bg: \'bg-blue-50\',\\n    text: \'text-blue-700\',\\n    border: \'border-blue-200\',\\n    badgeBg: \'bg-blue-50\',\\n    badgeText: \'text-blue-700 border-blue-200/70\',\\n    dot: \'bg-blue-500\',\\n  },\\n  Donn\303\251es: {\\n    bg: \'bg-emerald-50\',\\n    text: \'text-emerald-700\',\\n    border: \'border-emerald-200\',\\n    badgeBg: \'bg-emerald-50\',\\n    badgeText: \'text-emerald-700 border-emerald-200/70\',\\n    dot: \'bg-emerald-500\',\\n  },\\n  Fonctions: {\\n    bg: \'bg-purple-50\',\\n    text: \'text-purple-700\',\\n    border: \'border-purple-200\',\\n    badgeBg: \'bg-purple-50\',\\n    badgeText: \'text-purple-700 border-purple-200/70\',\\n    dot: \'bg-purple-500\',\\n  },\\n  POO: {\\n    bg: \'bg-amber-50\',\\n    text: \'text-amber-800\',\\n    border: \'border-amber-200\',\\n    badgeBg: \'bg-amber-50\',\\n    badgeText: \'text-amber-800 border-amber-200/70\',\\n    dot: \'bg-amber-500\',\\n  },\\n  Architecture: {\\n    bg: \'bg-cyan-50\',\\n    text: \'text-cyan-800\',\\n    border: \'border-cyan-200\',\\n    badgeBg: \'bg-cyan-50\',\\n    badgeText: \'text-cyan-800 border-cyan-200/70\',\\n    dot: \'bg-cyan-500\',\\n  },\\n  Fichiers: {\\n    bg: \'bg-rose-50\',\\n    text: \'text-rose-700\',\\n    border: \'border-rose-200\',\\n    badgeBg: \'bg-rose-50\',\\n    badgeText: \'text-rose-700 border-rose-200/70\',\\n    dot: \'bg-rose-500\',\\n  },\\n  \'Data Science\': {\\n    bg: \'bg-indigo-50\',\\n    text: \'text-indigo-700\',\\n    border: \'border-indigo-200\',\\n    badgeBg: \'bg-indigo-50\',\\n    badgeText: \'text-indigo-700 border-indigo-200/70\',\\n    dot: \'bg-indigo-500\',\\n  },\\n};\\n\\nexport const DEFAULT_CATEGORY_STYLE = {\\n  bg: \'bg-gray-100\',\\n  text: \'text-gray-700\',\\n  border: \'border-gray-200\',\\n  badgeBg: \'bg-gray-100\',\\n  badgeText: \'text-gray-700 border-gray-200\',\\n  dot: \'bg-gray-400\',\\n};\\n\\n// Explications p\303\251dagogiques et bonnes pratiques pour enrichir la fiche\\nexport const CARD_EXPLANATIONS: Record<number, { explanation: string; tip: string }> = {\\n  1: {\\n    explanation: \\\"input() retourne toujours une cha\303\256ne de caract\303\250res (str). Il faut explicitement convertir avec int() ou float() pour les calculs num\303\251riques.\\\",\\n    tip: \\\"Astuce : print() accepte sep=\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\" et end=\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\" pour contr\303\264ler les s\303\251parateurs et le saut de ligne.\\\"\\n  },\\n  2: {\\n    explanation: \\\"L\'indentation (g\303\251n\303\251ralement 4 espaces) d\303\251finit les blocs de code en Python. range(debut, fin, pas) exclut la valeur finale.\\\",\\n    tip: \\\"Astuce : range(1, 10, 2) g\303\251n\303\250re [1, 3, 5, 7, 9].\\\"\\n  },\\n  3: {\\n    explanation: \\\"Python est \303\240 typage dynamique fort : les types ne sont pas implicitement convertis lors d\'op\303\251rations incompatibles.\\\",\\n    tip: \\\"Astuce : bool(\'\') ou bool(0) valent False (valeurs Falsy).\\\"\\n  },\\n  4: {\\n    explanation: \\\"Les tuples sont immuables (prot\303\251g\303\251s contre les modifications accidentelles) et peuvent servir de cl\303\251s de dictionnaires contrairement aux listes.\\\",\\n    tip: \\\"Astuce : Pour un tuple \303\240 un seul \303\251l\303\251ment, ajoutez une virgule : t = (42,).\\\"\\n  },\\n  5: {\\n    explanation: \\\"Le d\303\251coupage (slicing) [debut:fin:pas] permet d\'extraire des sous-listes sans modifier la liste originale. L[::-1] renvoie une copie invers\303\251e.\\\",\\n    tip: \\\"Astuce : L.append(x) modifie la liste en place et renvoie None.\\\"\\n  },\\n  6: {\\n    explanation: \\\"Les dictionnaires associent des cl\303\251s uniques \303\240 des valeurs. La recherche par cl\303\251 est en temps constant O(1).\\\",\\n    tip: \\\"Astuce : Utilisez d.get(\'cle\', valeur_par_defaut) pour \303\251viter un KeyError.\\\"\\n  },\\n  7: {\\n    explanation: \\\"Les annotations de type (type hints) aident les IDEs et mypy sans affecter l\'ex\303\251cution runtime. Les lambdas sont des fonctions anonymes d\'une seule expression.\\\",\\n    tip: \\\"Astuce : Privil\303\251giez \'def\' plut\303\264t qu\'une lambda assign\303\251e \303\240 une variable pour la clart\303\251.\\\"\\n  },\\n  8: {\\n    explanation: \\\"Fonctions d\'ordre sup\303\251rieur du paradigme fonctionnel. map et filter renvoient des it\303\251rateurs, n\303\251cessitant list() pour \303\252tre mat\303\251rialis\303\251s.\\\",\\n    tip: \\\"Astuce : Les list comprehensions [x*x for x in L] sont souvent pr\303\251f\303\251r\303\251es en Python moderne.\\\"\\n  },\\n  9: {\\n    explanation: \\\"self repr\303\251sente l\'instance courante de la classe. __init__ est la m\303\251thode sp\303\251ciale appel\303\251e lors de l\'instanciation.\\\",\\n    tip: \\\"Astuce : Toutes les m\303\251thodes d\'instance doivent d\303\251clarer \'self\' comme premier argument.\\\"\\n  },\\n  10: {\\n    explanation: \\\"try / except permet de g\303\251rer les erreurs proprement. Le bloc \'finally\' est toujours ex\303\251cut\303\251, m\303\252me en cas d\'exception non intercept\303\251e.\\\",\\n    tip: \\\"Astuce : \303\211vitez le \'except:\' nu, sp\303\251cifiez toujours le type d\'exception attendu.\\\"\\n  },\\n  11: {\\n    explanation: \\\"__name__ == \'__main__\' permet d\'ex\303\251cuter du code uniquement lorsque le script est lanc\303\251 directement, et non lorsqu\'il est import\303\251.\\\",\\n    tip: \\\"Astuce : Indispensable pour cr\303\251er des scripts r\303\251utilisables sous forme de modules.\\\"\\n  },\\n  12: {\\n    explanation: \\\"Le module os interagit avec le syst\303\250me d\'exploitation et les chemins de fichiers. Shutil g\303\250re les op\303\251rations de haut niveau comme la copie de fichiers.\\\",\\n    tip: \\\"Astuce : En Python moderne (>=3.4), le module pathlib.Path est souvent une excellente alternative.\\\"\\n  },\\n  13: {\\n    explanation: \\\"Le gestionnaire de contexte \'with\' garantit la fermeture automatique du fichier, m\303\252me si une exception survient pendant la lecture/\303\251criture.\\\",\\n    tip: \\\"Astuce : Pr\303\251cisez encoding=\\\\\\\"utf-8\\\\\\\" lors de l\'ouverture pour \303\251viter les probl\303\250mes d\'encodage sous Windows.\\\"\\n  },\\n  14: {\\n    explanation: \\\"NumPy vectorise les calculs math\303\251matiques pour des performances C ultra-rapides sur des tableaux \303\240 N dimensions.\\\",\\n    tip: \\\"Astuce : Les op\303\251rations arithm\303\251tiques (+, *, etc.) s\'appliquent \303\251l\303\251ment par \303\251l\303\251ment.\\\"\\n  },\\n  15: {\\n    explanation: \\\"Pandas est l\'outil standard pour la manipulation tabulaire en Data Science. loc[] filtre par label et index, iloc[] par position num\303\251rique.\\\",\\n    tip: \\\"Astuce : Utilisez df.head() et df.info() pour inspecter rapidement un jeu de donn\303\251es.\\\"\\n  },\\n  16: {\\n    explanation: \\\"Matplotlib est la biblioth\303\250que fondamentale de visualisation en Python. Chaque fonction configure la figure courante avant plt.show().\\\",\\n    tip: \\\"Astuce : Enregistrez votre graphique avec plt.savefig(\'graph.png\', dpi=300).\\\"\\n  }\\n};\\n\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/constants.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating styling constants and explanations\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create constants.ts\"}"
